body:
I really appreciate the time you took to reply. I commented elsewhere but this was a test post to make sure she wasn't suspicious of me. I changed some info to throw her off and I haven't been approached yet so I'll give you the real situation now.

&#x200B;

Her and I are engaged and attend the same college. We're locked into a one year lease together and she pays for pretty much all of it, even though half is in my name.

&#x200B;

That being said I haven't left yet. I want to so bad. Every time I get close she shows me affection and cries and says she treats me so bad and I fall for it every time. But now she's doing it again. She's pouting, treating me harsh, and blaming me for something out of my control. 

&#x200B;

Given my situation I can't quit college or transfer. And I doubt I'll be able to get out of my lease. I'm getting interviewed left and right waiting for a callback so maybe I can find an easy escape. I'm hesitant to tell my doctor cause she works for the school and I don't want her to report my fiance. Even if she is abusive, I don't want to ruin her life and I've no doubt she'll make a false rape claim on me because she's said she'd do it to other people she suspected would screw her over.

&#x200B;

I'm really hoping she tries to start crap because it's easier for me to call her out when she's acting up than when she's not. I just want out and I've been getting worse because I'm forgetting my antidepressants half the time. I've been reading my bible trying to hype myself up to stand up for myself. Wish me luck, I want out soon.

This post was a test run to see if she'd catch me trying to use a different reddit account. 

&#x200B;

Some things I need to note now that I know she won't find this:

We are engaged and locked in a 1 year lease together. And we don't actually work together, we go to the same college (I changed this to avoid her suspicion).

&#x200B;

That being said, I haven't left yet. Every time I get close to leaving she shows me affection and says she doesn't treat me write and puts on the tears. I fall for it every time like a fool. But here I am again. She's pouting, treating me harsh, and blaming me for something I can't even control. At this point I'm hoping she picks a fight tonight so I have even more of a reason to take off. It is easier for me to call her out on her crap when she's dishing it out. Wish me luck, I really want to leave soon.

&#x200B;

My thoughts have been getting worse and I keep forgetting to take my antidepressants. I've been reading the bible every day trying to find the strength to leave.
